      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 64-year-old female presented with pulmonary edema and cardiogenic shock after coronary arteriography that showed severe subocclusive lesion in the left main coronary artery (LMCA) in a dominant left coronary system. The patient successfully underwent urgent angioplasty with stent deployment in the LMCA. After an uneventful period, the patient was discharged at day six."},
